From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Srinivas Kandagatla <srinivas.kandagatla@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 17:48:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] ASoC: codecs: lpass-rx-macro: handle version 2.9 and
 sm8550 NPL clock

Add LPASS_CODEC_VERSION_2_9 to the version-based switch statements so
it is handled the same as other 2.5-family variants (including Glymur).

Also add LPASS_MACRO_FLAG_HAS_NPL_CLOCK to the sm8550 match entry; the
missing flag left sm8550 running without its NPL clock and caused
sporadic playback stalls.

Signed-off-by: Srinivas Kandagatla <srinivas.kandagatla@oss.qualcomm.com>
(cherry picked from commit 0496ea850258a5d0e36cf5e2d2e0cef30b1e3045)
(cherry picked from commit c47735063b63ded1cd56313e9b2406d90cf7f592)
---
 sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
index 0d5ea75e5018..dbca28a6891d 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
@@ -3991,6 +3991,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id rx_macro_dt_match[] = {
 		.data = (void *)LPASS_MACRO_FLAG_HAS_NPL_CLOCK,
 	}, {
 		.compatible = "qcom,sm8550-lpass-rx-macro",
+		.data = (void *)LPASS_MACRO_FLAG_HAS_NPL_CLOCK,
 	}, {
 		.compatible = "qcom,sc8280xp-lpass-rx-macro",
 		.data = (void *)LPASS_MACRO_FLAG_HAS_NPL_CLOCK,
